  "format": "ai-tools",
  "script": "ChatGPT just learned to keep your face.\n\nThis month OpenAI rebuilt its image editor: it holds your face steady through an edit, and it follows a long instruction without breaking it.\n\nHere's why nine prompts are going viral: the sentence you write decides the shot.\n\nPaste one in with your selfie, and ChatGPT builds the shoot.\n\nDSLR Photographer Mode names a camera, a location, a depth of field.\n\nStill, it reads like a real portrait session, not a filter.\n\nGolden Hour Photo Shoot: same face, warm light, natural shadows.\n\nThat's the shot that once needed a photographer and an hour of sun.\n\nRestoring Old Photos runs it backwards.\n\nSharpen, relight, rebuild a scan into something shot today.\n\nThat same line closes every prompt: keep the face, keep the skin natural.\n\nSkip it, and the result is the plastic AI look everyone already spots.\n\nThere are nine of these.\n\nComment PROMPTS and they're yours.",
